# PART 1 — SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE

Build the application using four independent architectural layers.

### Layer 1: User Interface

Contains:

- Dashboard
- Daily Journal
- Sessions
- Trades
- Calendar
- Analytics
- Reviews
- Live Engagement
- Settings and Export

This layer can be redesigned or redeveloped without affecting personal records.

### Layer 2: Application Logic

Contains:

- Trading calculations
- Session lifecycle management
- Trade lifecycle management
- Event recording
- Analytics calculations
- Validation rules
- Account management
- Import and export operations

This layer must follow a stable set of documented business rules.

### Layer 3: Data Storage

Contains all persistent personal records:

- User profile
- Trading accounts
- Daily journals
- Trading sessions
- Trade records
- Session event timelines
- Trade event timelines
- Screenshots and attachments
- Session templates
- Checklists
- Instruments
- Preferences
- Settings

This layer must operate independently of the application deployment.

### Layer 4: Universal Data Portability

A dedicated data exchange system that allows personal records to move between compatible versions of ATK Deck and Hyper Tracker.

It must use a documented, versioned data format.

It must not require the two applications to communicate with one another.

