# PART 7 — COMPLETE DATA INDEPENDENCE

ATK Deck Personal and Hyper Tracker Commercial must remain completely separate.

This is a strict architectural requirement.

### No automatic connections

Do not implement:

- Live database sharing.
- Cross-website data synchronisation.
- Automatic account linking.
- Shared workspace access.
- Background cross-application imports.
- Automatic record propagation.

### Separate databases

ATK Deck Personal must use its own independent database and storage.

Hyper Tracker Commercial must use its own separate database and storage.

Each deployment must have:

- Separate database credentials.
- Separate authentication configuration.
- Separate storage permissions.
- Separate environment variables.
- Separate deployment configuration.

The applications may implement the same data standard, but they must never share a live database.

### Manual migration only

Example:

ATK Deck Personal → Export backup → Download ZIP → Hyper Tracker Commercial → Import backup.

The reverse must work equally well.

Once imported, the destination maintains its own independent copy.

Changes made afterward in one application must not appear in the other.

